WEBVTT

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.940
What? You're going to quit being a host?

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:46.950
Yes, I'm going to quit and 
open a plastic model shop.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:50.040
I already have the perfect name.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.780
Plastic Kyoshiro.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.890
Uh, what are you talking about, Kyoshiro-san?

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:57.610
That wasn't funny. Who's going 
to recognize that reference?

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:02.400
Yeah, you should open a Mini 4WD 
store called Dash Kyoshiro instead.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:03.780
Nobody's going to recognize that one either!

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.590
What's wrong anyway?

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:07.550
You're the number one host 
in the Kabuki district.

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:09.430
Is the silicon in your 
nose starting to crumble?

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.680
I feel like I've hit a wall,

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:15.340
so I wanted to invite the members of

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:17.560
Odd Jobs to be my final customers.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:22.440
Hold on. Has all the plastic 
surgery damaged your brain?

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.660
If the head is too light, the 
car will rise on sharp turns

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:28.950
and you'll fly off the track, 
so you'll need side rollers...

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.830
Stop talking about Mini 4WDs!

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.070
Hachiro-san, what happened?

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:38.180
Do you know Madame Yagami?

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:38.960
Hachiro!

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:43.470
She's said to be an Edo-born socialite, 
and something of an enigma.

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:48.920
A tip of her glass and the balance 
of power in this town crumbles.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:54.710
Whoever controls her 
controls the night streets.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:58.890
She descends like a goddess 
of fortune in the dark

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:01.360
and leaves wealth and riches in her wake.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.190
But she never visits the same town again.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:07.480
A goddess of the night.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.910
And a few nights ago,

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:15.620
the Madame visited Takamagahara.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:19.040
What? Isn't that great?

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.480
Like when a pro Mini 4WD racer 
shows up at a local tournament?

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:24.840
That's kind of hard to relate to.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:27.850
However, the Madame had a message

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.750
for us when she left.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:37.660
I'll be back next week at the same time.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:41.210
Huh? Th-That's terrific!

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:43.340
You secured a promise from someone who

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:44.810
never visits the same place twice!

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.110
No, this is not a good thing.

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:47.610
Huh?

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:50.330
The Madame is aware that she

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.110
has the power to completely reshape a town.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:56.650
Which is why she shuns every club,

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:59.640
even the ones she takes a liking to.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.620
When the Madame says that 
she will be returning,

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:06.630
she intends to ruin us.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.900
Tomorrow, she will no longer 
be a goddess of fortune,

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.630
but a goddess of death.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:17.130
Wh-Why?!

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:19.520
Did something happen to upset her?

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:22.520
We're talking about the most 
powerful socialite under the sun.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:25.270
I would assume that she didn't like 
some aspect of the experience.

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:28.350
So you don't actually want to quit.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:30.480
You just think that this 
place will be shut down.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:33.280
Speaking of which, I don't 
see any other hosts around.

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:38.530
Yes, they're all too scared to work.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.560
I'm very sorry.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:44.290
Our failure will ruin the entire town.

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:47.670
But while I've given up on the club,

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:50.750
I won't let her ruin this town.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.300
I swear on my pride as a host.

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:55.350
But how are we supposed to entertain the

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:56.850
Madame when everyone's gone?

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.830
Nevertheless, we must do

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:01.120
what we can to curry the Madame's favor.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.280
How many?

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:02.680
Huh?

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:07.360
How many dashing, young men do you require?

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:09.440
And...

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:15.450
Are you positive that she's rich, boss?

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:21.450
<b>We Are All Hosts, In Capital Letters</b>

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:25.670
Listen up!

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:27.350
We're going to scout the Kabuki district for

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:31.000
Hunks of the Zodiac to take on the Madame!

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:32.790
Everyone ready?

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.050
Just do it!

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.300
Sparkling!

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:36.950
Okay!

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.650
My life is yours.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.520
Consider it done.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:48.150
Ignore anyone below a Bronze Saint.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:50.250
Ideally, we want Silver Saints.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.230
Excuse me! I have no idea 
what that means! Whoo-hoo!

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:57.420
In other words, we don't want 
anyone uglier than Isao Hashizume,

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:01.010
and anyone more handsome than 
Makoto Fujita is too handsome,

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:02.850
so reject them too!

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:04.960
You just eliminated the 
majority of the human race!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:08.000
What's the difference 
between bronze and silver?!

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:09.290
In other words,

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:13.200
make sure you don't bring any Gold Saints

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.210
like Masaharu Fukuyama or Shun Oguri.

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:20.850
They'll make us look bad 
and scare the customers.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:23.160
So you want us to bring ugly people?!

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.520
Just go!

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:27.360
Uh... Excuse me, Odd Jobs.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:32.260
I appreciate the help, but 
this isn't such an easy job.

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:34.480
Looks are only a starting point.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:38.280
Hosts must have personalities 
that draw people to them.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:43.780
So you're saying that I'm 
all looks and no substance?

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:44.910
Just a pretty face?

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:46.870
Uh, I never said that.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:49.460
And I never said that you 
were particularly handsome.

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:57.050
In other words, it's what's 
inside that counts.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:06:58.670
E-Er, I guess...

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:01.500
And that's what we're focused on.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.850
Gin-san, I heard you had a job for me.

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:05.430
Huh?

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:07.790
This is worse than I expected!

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.440
And is he wearing paper?!

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:11.310
Hold on a second.

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:27.450
<b>I want to meet Jang Geun-suk.</b>

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:13.970
Wouldn't he considered a Cardboard Saint?

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:15.570
This isn't cardboard.

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:20.520
Look, I also used newspaper 
and colorful t-shirts.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.120
It's kind of like a suit.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.960
No, it's not.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:27.450
And your necklace is somebody's 
Tanabata wish card.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:29.420
Sorry, boss.

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:33.610
I was aiming for a hosty, flashy look.

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:36.040
Uh, do you understand what 
it means to be a host?

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:38.460
He may not look like much on the outside,

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:40.250
but he's a hard worker on the inside.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:42.340
Like a J Leaguer.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:44.190
Welcome aboard!

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:48.600
Look, he's even sporting 
a sponsor on his back.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:48.350
<b>Aomori Apples</b>

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:51.750
And he's got bling around his neck.

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:53.980
And we're planning a 
shotgun wedding with Rosa!

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:57.380
U-Uh, Odd Jobs?

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:01.070
We work in the service industry, 
so I need someone more...

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:05.620
Don't worry. I've got it covered.

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:08.580
I happen to know this handsome fellow 
who works in the service industry.

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.990
And I'm not talking about 
one of those metrosexuals

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.510
that are all the rage these days.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:14.450
This one's a real macho...

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:16.790
Did you just call me macho?!

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:17.840
Sis!

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:22.470
Shin-chan, explain yourself.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.630
I came because you told me

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:27.180
that Hideyoshi's lost 
treasure had been found!

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:28.960
Y-You've got it wrong, Sis!

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:31.330
I was saying that we could obtain wealth

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:33.210
that would rival Hideyoshi's lost treasure,

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:34.980
so just bear with us.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:36.610
Shut your mouth!

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:39.630
Why should I dress up like a 
man and work at a host club?!

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:41.470
See, she's so manly.

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:42.740
Listen to me, Otae!

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:44.860
There isn't much difference between 
a hostess club and a host club!

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:46.450
The only difference is the gender!

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:47.970
Which means you're already a host...

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.810
P-Please calm yourself, Otae-san.

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:52.750
You have it all wrong.

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:56.560
I thought that the top hostess 
in the Kabuki district...

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:57.250
Huh?

00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:01.800
...would be able to introduce 
us to some handsome men.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:03.880
Since you must be very popular with the guys.

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:06.390
Huh? O-Oh...

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:09.390
Please, Kyoshiro-san!

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:13.060
Boss!

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:15.120
Handsome men?

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:19.390
I suppose that I know a few.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:20.770
Who should I choose?

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:21.940
This is so difficult!

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:24.930
Oh, Otae-san. Did you need me for something?

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.430
And here comes someone who was 
never invited to the party!

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:29.530
Why is he acting like we 
begged him to come here?!

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:31.070
I want to punch him in the face!

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:34.050
I understand, Otae-san.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:36.000
You didn't want to ask me to be a host

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.210
because you didn't want to risk losing me

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.150
to some other girl, right?

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:42.470
I saw it all transpire.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.460
Nothing like that ever happened!

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:46.470
How long have you been 
watching us, you stalker?!

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:51.290
Don't worry. Nobody can steal my heart.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:55.190
Isao will forever be your personal hostalker.

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:58.100
<b>Host + Stalker = Hostalker</b>

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:58.100
Nobody would want you as a personal host.

00:09:58.480 --> 00:09:59.480
Hostcar?

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:00.980
Hey, guys.

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:03.770
This guy wants a host's car.

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:05.040
We can have him carry our stuff.

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.740
Wait! That's not what I said!

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.900
We've got enough people now.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:10.450
Let's head back, boys!

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:15.200
U-Uh, excuse me.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:19.190
I would like everyone to 
take an aptitude test.

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:20.860
Aptitude test?

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:25.530
Yes, since a host's job 
is to chat with girls.

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:32.670
I would like all of you to talk to 
girls and bring them to the club.

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:35.960
You can pretend that you're 
trying to pick up the girls.

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:41.330
At first glance, hosts may 
appear to operate solo,

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:45.150
but that's only when customers 
request you by name.

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:50.210
Temporary help typically 
plays a supporting role.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:52.490
In other words, teamwork is critical.

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:57.730
Show me that you can cover 
for each other's mistakes

00:10:57.730 --> 00:10:59.630
and accomplish your job.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.270
Is that their target?

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:05.210
Oh, excuse me.

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:07.380
He bumped into her to 
create an excuse to talk.

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:09.640
Oh, no. I wasn't paying attention.

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:11.830
Uh, excuse me...

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.890
I believe this dropped from your back.

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:16.880
Feather.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:19.000
Uh, you're the one who 
just dropped everything!

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:24.270
<b>I want to meet Jang Geun-suk.</b>

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:21.890
The suit fell apart when he bumped into her!

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:23.260
Somebody help him!

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:24.270
Oh, sorry.

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:26.830
That belongs to me.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.260
How is that supposed to help?!

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:30.260
And that feather was yours?!

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:34.170
Uh, she looks more like an angel to me.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:35.840
No, I'm the angel.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.470
Well, can you prove it?

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:40.500
Don't you people have more important 
things to be talking about?!

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:42.510
Hey! What are you people doing?!

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.100
Crap! It's the police!

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.420
They can't pick up girls now!

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:46.960
Why not use rock, paper, scissors

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:48.300
to decide?

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:50.000
You're joining in?!

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.840
Why do you people keep striking funny poses?!

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:56.700
Okay. We'll use rock, paper, scissors 
to determine who the feather belongs to.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:59.320
Um, I'm not an angel.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:00.940
Just do as we say.

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:02.470
Um, I'm in a hurry.

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:05.210
Hey! You're scaring her off!

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:07.480
Well, you should just give it a try.

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:09.110
As I've been saying...

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:12.560
I'm not an angel!

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:13.740
You too!

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:16.330
What was the point of this entire exchange?!

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:16.330
We're sorry!

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:18.990
It was nothing more than a sham!

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:24.380
What is with those people?

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:26.050
There must be something wrong with them.

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:27.170
You're absolutely right.

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:29.480
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:31.570
No, don't be.

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:34.200
I'm the one who approached you.

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:35.660
C-Could it be?!

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:36.800
This is the main event?!

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:40.420
Th-Then I'll be going now!

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:42.060
Ah, please wait.

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:43.180
Huh?

00:12:43.180 --> 00:12:48.400
So the entire sequence was 
one giant accident designed

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:51.000
to create an opening in her heart?!

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:54.570
You dropped this. It's not a feather.

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:57.450
Huh? This is...

00:12:57.450 --> 00:12:58.950
I-I'm sorry.

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:02.710
But I would love to

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:05.960
talk with you again.

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:11.820
Well, if you happen to have some time,

00:13:11.820 --> 00:13:14.130
feel free to drop by.

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:15.140
As luck would have it,

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:17.470
I'm always available since 
no one ever asks for me.

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:21.060
And he used a subtle invitation 
instead of a direct one

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:23.480
to soften the bad rep that 
comes with being a host!

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:26.230
S-So you're a host.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:29.230
No, I might be the devil.

00:13:29.230 --> 00:13:33.100
And then he shows his wild side?!

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:39.200
U-Um, I-I might visit your club then,

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:42.910
just to see what it's like, I guess...

00:13:42.910 --> 00:13:47.500
I invite you to Takamagahara, 
a refuge for angels.

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:49.780
He landed her?!

00:13:49.780 --> 00:13:52.970
They were able to recover 
from that horrible beginning!

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:56.010
No, this was all part of their plan!

00:13:56.010 --> 00:14:00.510
Maybe... Just maybe they can pull it off!

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:03.130
The club is nearby, so allow 
me to escort you there.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:05.940
It wouldn't do to let an 
angel get her feet dirty.

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.110
You're too kind...

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:11.270
They may be able to put up a 
fight against the Madame!

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:11.980
Now.

00:14:11.980 --> 00:14:13.650
Vroom!

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:15.110
Please get on.

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:20.800
What's wrong? You've never 
seen a hostcar before?

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:21.660
Vroom!

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:24.190
It's a comfortable ride.

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:25.360
Down, boy.

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:26.820
Hey, stop it.

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:27.900
Hold up now.

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:28.670
You're going the wrong way!

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:31.000
<b>Dream Castle</b>

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.790
Come on now.

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:35.230
This is a completely 
different kind of refuge.

00:14:35.230 --> 00:14:37.120
Seriously.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:38.130
Oh, well.

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:40.340
Let's go inside for a bit...

00:14:40.430 --> 00:14:46.350
<b>Shinsengumi</b>

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:44.480
Help! Police!

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:46.350
That host is very weird!

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:51.230
What's wrong with you?

00:14:51.860 --> 00:14:53.340
What's wrong with you?

00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:54.480
Yeah!

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:57.470
We're just your average weird hosts!

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:13.410
Uh, I asked you guys to bring customers.

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:16.440
Why did you get yourself arrested?

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:17.380
Boss.

00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:20.370
We would have landed two or three girls

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:23.700
if it wasn't for these rotten cops.

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:25.260
Ain't that right, ISAO?

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:27.920
GIN is absolutely right.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:32.460
Cops are getting so anal these days.

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:34.570
It's getting hard to live in this town.

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:36.810
You're in charge of those cops!

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:38.630
That's ancient history.

00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:42.790
I've abandoned my position 
and prestige for Otae-san

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:47.930
to start over from the bottom 
of society as a hostalker!

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:53.170
Kondo-san, I think you'll be 
starting from the Jomon period.

00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:55.360
We're leaving.

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:57.380
If you want a job as a car, 
you can be a patrol car

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:58.940
that helps keep the streets safe.

00:15:58.940 --> 00:16:01.630
Hosts also keep the streets safe!

00:16:01.630 --> 00:16:05.680
If we don't do anything, that 
Madame will ruin this town!

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:08.060
What are you babbling about?

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:10.390
GIN! Help me out here!

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:12.370
This club will be in trouble without its ace!

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:15.560
Whitebeard and Luffy won't stand for this!

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:18.900
Just feed him one banana a day.

00:16:18.900 --> 00:16:21.570
If he still runs slow, have 
him hold his own banana.

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:22.680
No!

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:24.850
I'll be turned into a circus show gorilla!

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:26.470
Stop struggling and come with us!

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:28.080
Boss!

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:29.950
Uh, could you wait a moment?

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.290
Boss!

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:33.550
No, I wasn't talking to the gorilla.

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:37.340
This could very well be...

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:39.840
This could very well be it!

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:42.300
<b>Takamagahara</b>

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.570
What? Really?

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:46.010
You bet!

00:16:46.010 --> 00:16:49.610
Ladies, do you have any plans tonight?

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:53.800
If not, why not drop by Takamagahara,

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:57.230
the refuge for angels, to rest your wings?

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:01.420
Huh? Takamagahara's open again?

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:05.780
I heard that they were closed 
because a bunch of hosts quit.

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:06.570
Yeah.

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:10.370
The club has reopened with many new hosts.

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:11.630
Really?

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:14.560
But the new hosts are probably ugly.

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:15.750
I bet.

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:17.460
Absolutely not.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:20.300
The hosts here are all handsome men

00:17:20.300 --> 00:17:22.770
selected from all over Edo.

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:26.390
I promise that they will make 
this a very magical night.

00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:30.470
Welcome.

00:17:30.470 --> 00:17:32.390
To New Takamagahara.

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:36.620
You won't be getting any sleep 
tonight, my little pussy cats.

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:39.400
We're gonna have a HOT and COOL party here.

00:17:40.190 --> 00:17:42.480
Here we go!

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:44.390
Let's party!

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:46.280
Okay!

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:48.660
Hell no!

00:17:48.930 --> 00:17:52.290
Why are we partying?!

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:55.120
When did Kondo-san turn 
into Harley Gorillason?!

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:58.060
You definitely fit the part.

00:17:58.060 --> 00:18:00.220
My eyes haven't failed me.

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:01.970
Please.

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:06.550
I need your help to protect 
this town from the Madame.

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:08.280
Screw that.

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:10.690
Samurai do not fool around.

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:14.150
The Shinsengumi are obligated 
to protect this town,

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:15.880
so this is our duty!

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:19.510
I don't think it's our duty 
to wear handles on our heads.

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:21.270
This is an order from your chief.

00:18:21.270 --> 00:18:23.730
We're partying all night!

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:26.820
There's a party in your 
head every single day!

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:29.140
Now, now. Calm down.

00:18:29.140 --> 00:18:30.720
Get yourself a drink,

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:31.580
TOSHI.

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:33.250
Don't call me TOSHI!

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:35.580
And why are you already 
entertaining customers?!

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.550
I'm not sure what this is about,

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.240
but I've figured out how this works.

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:42.660
I just have to trick dumb 
bitches into giving me money

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:44.780
while I eat and drink for free.

00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:48.500
Aw, SOUGO is so mean!

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:52.220
Sorry. I wasn't talking about you.

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:55.600
Because you alone are special.

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:59.240
Excuse me! Another bottle of Dom Perignon!

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:00.730
He's a natural!

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:01.930
This job was made for him!

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:04.110
He's shining in all his evil glory!

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:06.040
Well, in any case,

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:08.060
I'll be serving the Madame.

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:11.240
The two of them will be my help.

00:19:11.240 --> 00:19:14.370
The rest of you will be help for the help.

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:16.420
Why would you need help for the help?!

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:18.670
Even the Beatles didn't use that much help!

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:20.460
Screw that!

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:22.450
I'm not going to be reduced to help for them!

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:25.990
He basically looks like 
Shinpachi without the glasses!

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:26.930
Yeah!

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:29.770
Yeah, if Gin-chan dyed his hair 
black, they would look the same!

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:31.890
My face isn't that dumb!

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:33.320
What?!

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:36.330
You're getting a cocky 
because you rose two places

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:38.380
in the third character poll.

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:40.520
I might not be so popular in 2D,

00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:43.530
but in 3D, everyone wants me!

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.640
Could you stop fighting?!

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:47.400
And what does 3D have to do with anything?!

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:48.370
I don't need any lip from the

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:50.650
person who's miraculously placed 
8th three times in a row!

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:55.190
Fool. You're lucky the 
author sucks at drawing.

00:19:55.190 --> 00:19:58.850
In 3D, you would look like Yo Oizumi.

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:00.210
A hairball!

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:02.320
Calm down, Hijikata-san!

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:04.170
What's so bad about Yo Oizumi?!

00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:05.670
Shut up, Hat Trick!

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:10.760
What?! In 3D, you would look 
like Daisuke Sakaguchi!

00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:11.910
That's me!

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:15.640
That's bullshit! Even his 
glasses look like the number 8!

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:17.460
All glasses look like the number 8!

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:19.240
Cut this out now!

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:21.600
Eight is for my name, my 
glasses, my 8th place...

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:25.640
Please. Stop fighting.

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:27.870
Everyone should get along.

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:30.070
Teamwork is important for hosts.

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:32.010
You're absolutely right.

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:34.700
We need to work together 
to satisfy the Madame.

00:20:35.310 --> 00:20:38.320
If you follow my instructions, we'll be fine.

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:40.360
I normally don't need help,

00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:42.960
so I'll try to do as much as I can myself.

00:20:43.550 --> 00:20:46.760
Otae-san, we'll send the 
customers home at 9 PM.

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:49.210
I want every person on 
standby for the Madame.

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:52.330
Er, you don't want any 
other customers around?

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:54.300
Yes, is there a problem?

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:57.970
Sorry, I thought you wanted some excitement,

00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:00.530
so I invited a lot of people.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:08.110
Ooh! It's been so long, Kyoshiro-sama!

00:21:09.610 --> 00:21:12.810
Thank you for the invitation.

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:15.050
You must have really missed us.

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:18.100
Kyoshiro-sama is so happy that 
he's foaming at the mouth!

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:19.130
I love it!

00:21:19.760 --> 00:21:21.060
Fabulous!

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:23.500
It's the Saigo trannies!

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:25.150
Hey, Otae.

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:27.630
Is it true that you're footing the bill?

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:32.050
Yes, we're going all out 
to celebrate the reopening.

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:34.260
Uh, nobody gave you 
permission to do that, Sis!

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:39.030
Okay! We'll be drinking 'til 
morning, Kyoshiro-sama!

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:41.640
Wait! Kyoshiro-san!

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:41.360
Enjoy yourselves.

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:45.430
H-Help...

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:49.210
The Madame isn't even here and 
he's already asking for help.

00:21:49.210 --> 00:21:51.440
No, he's literally asking for help,

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:54.860
as in "oh my god help me 
please," so we can ignore him.

00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:56.410
We can't ignore him!

00:21:56.910 --> 00:21:59.840
And the Madame is about to come!

00:22:00.240 --> 00:22:01.910
We haven't even started,

00:22:02.120 --> 00:22:06.840
and Kyoshiro-san has already been 
hunted down by the monsters!

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:09.060
Help...

00:22:07.920 --> 00:22:09.960
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:23:40.380 --> 00:23:44.930
